> 1. Which class do you think is the easiest to play, and why?
Healers. Use the starting potions, pets, and spells of healing and
stone to flesh.
If you are patient and level up carefully, they are quite easy to play.
Just avoid
the minegaurd and handle the mimics/floating eyes. Just avoid killing
anything
except for the mimics and floating eyes. Let the pets do the rest of
your work.
I prefer to do the Sokoban before the Minetown, to avoid the minetown
guard.
The only caveat is an early trap. Using the stone to flesh you must
have a
whole pet army by the time you reach the minetown after sokoban. With
credit
cloning and vault raiding there may be enough money to get full
protection even at XL6.

> 2. Consider the choice of genociding spellcasters versus powerful melee
> monsters.
Genociding is useful for spellcasters. Powerful Melee Monsters can be
avoided by
avoiding Melee. Genociding too many monsters may trigger the problem of
summoning
hell.
> 3. Evaluate the usefulness of chaotic artifacts.
The only good chaotic artifacts are the two quest artifacts. The
longbow gives ammunition, and is useful for classes able to get expert
in bows. The key gives half damage, so is usable by everybody.

